    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "> What about explicitly making version required\r\n\r\nI don't know what kind of stuff you have in mind,\r\n\r\nbut after your comment, I read the code again.\r\n\r\n```js\r\nif (process.env.SHIPJS === 'true' && !process.env.VERSION) {\r\n```\r\n\r\nThat condition might not be understandable in a few months.\r\nWhat if we just change it to\r\n\r\n```js\r\nif (process.env.NODE_ENV === 'production' && !process.env.VERSION) {\r\n```\r\n\r\nShip.js prepends `NODE_ENV=production` and our previous release scripts did the same.\r\nOnly when we run `yarn build` on local machine, NODE_ENV is not `production`.\r\nSo it may be more explicit. What do you think?",
    "commit_id": "02a6f4d88648d609ec0327e0c4dc063ab7088a0e",
    "created_at": "2020-02-04T13:17:37Z",
